<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer_Register.xml   UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M6 build pass

  Registers RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer (Defs/MapGeneration/
  RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer.xml) onto Base_Player — identical shape to
  this same folder's own M1 precedent, Patches/
  RUT_Miasma_GradientAxis_Register.xml (PatchOperationConditional/
  PatchOperationAdd onto MapGeneratorDef[Base_Player]/genSteps, MayRequire
  on the added <li> itself so the cross-reference cannot dangle if either
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards or mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes is absent
  from the active mod list).

  🔴 WARDEN_MOTHER_BEFRIENDING_1: MayRequire updated from
  mandrake.rsw.swbestiary to mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes — the GenStepDef
  this registers now spawns RM_WardenMother (mandrake.rm.miasma) and her
  young from mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes juveniles, not the retired
  RSW_OpeeSeaKiller wiring placeholder.

  Global registration is deliberate and safe, mirroring that same file's
  own reasoning: RM_ScattererValidator_BrineShallowWater rejects every
  cell on every map whose biome carries no RM_GradientAxisExtension (i.e.
  every biome but the Miasma today), so this GenStep places nothing on any
  other biome's map — registering it once here, rather than needing a
  biome-specific MapGeneratorDef, is what lets a future second
  gradient-axis biome (M1's own header: "any future two-water biome does")
  get crèche placement for free too.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards,mandrake.rm.terminalbiomes">RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
